============================================================================================================
DELIVERABLE 1 -- WHAT VLBI CAN ACTUALLY REACH  (sigma_d = sigma_pi d^2)
============================================================================================================
  A parallax campaign of precision sigma_pi buys a DISTANCE precision
      sigma_d [pc] = sigma_pi [arcsec] * (d [pc])^2 ,
  because pi[arcsec] = 1/d[pc]. Sub-parsec is therefore a DISTANCE cut on the
  target, not a telescope-time cut. Floors used:
      sigma_pi = 13 uas -- DEMONSTRATED: Ding et al. (2024), J2222-0137, PX = 3.723 +/- 0.013 mas
      sigma_pi = 30 uas -- typical deep campaign

  sigma_pi = 13 uas : sub-parsec out to d =  277.4 pc ( 6 of 116 array pulsars) ; sub-lambda/2 out to  157.8 pc ( 3 pulsars)
  sigma_pi = 30 uas : sub-parsec out to d =  182.6 pc ( 3 of 116 array pulsars) ; sub-lambda/2 out to  103.9 pc ( 1 pulsars)

