============================================================================================================
DELIVERABLE 4 -- DIMINISHING RETURNS: THE VALUE OF ANCHOR #1, #2, ... #10
============================================================================================================
  GREEDY sequence: at each step take the pulsar with the largest marginal
  value GIVEN the anchors already bought. Reported in the ACHIEVABLE arm.

  STRUCTURAL WARNING, stated up front, because it changes what 'saturation' means:
    f_marg is EXACTLY separable -- it is sum_a R_a^2 pw_a / sum pw and R_a depends
      on pulsar a's prior alone. Its greedy curve IS the sorted cumulative sum, so
      any flattening is a statement about the VALUE DISTRIBUTION being heavy-tailed,
      NOT about anchors interacting. No anchor makes another anchor less useful.
    chirp mass has a separable FISHER but sigma = 1/sqrt(sum_a I_a) is not additive,
      so it gets a true greedy; the naive sorted cumsum overstates it ~2x.
    localisation genuinely COUPLES pulsars through the Schur complement, so it is
      the only product where a real interaction can appear. True greedy.

  f_marg (K=8): baseline 0.1833
    per-anchor : +1.379e-02 +6.959e-03 +6.521e-03 +6.032e-03 +5.691e-03 +5.347e-03 +2.429e-03 +1.663e-03 +1.626e-03 +1.515e-03
